msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: Groundwork Common, linked to the company site.
#: inc/admin-screen.php:611
#, php-format
msgid "%s provides technology leadership and support for nonprofits — fractional, by the project, or alongside an in-house team. We release tools like this one because good technology work should leave an organization more capable, not more dependent on whoever built it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:619
msgid "If you find this plugin useful, the most valuable thing you can do for us is mention us to a nonprofit who might benefit from our services. Referrals are how our business continues to grow its impact and reach."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:625
msgid "Learn about Groundwork Common"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:634
msgid "You can also support our WordPress plugins directly. While we offer the plugin free to you, it costs us to maintain it — the security updates, the compatibility testing against each new WordPress release, the bug nobody but you has hit. We can’t do it without your support, and we appreciate whatever support you can give."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-screen.php:639
msgid "Support our work"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:53
msgid "Organization name"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:55
msgid "Leave empty to use the site title."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:62
msgid "Address"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:63
msgid "Printed under the name. One line per line."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:69
msgid "Logo"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:70
msgid "Printed above the organization name. Kept small on purpose — this is correspondence, not a flyer. Email programs often refuse to load images, so the name is always printed as text underneath and the letter reads correctly without it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:76
msgid "Contact for questions"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:78
msgid "Where a court or school should direct questions about a letter. This is the number somebody phones to check a reference code, so make it one that is answered."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:87
msgid "Signed by"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:88
msgid "Printed under the signature line. Left empty, the line prints unlabeled — which looks unfinished, and is meant to."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:94
msgid "Their title"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:95
msgid "Printed under the name — \"Volunteer Coordinator\", \"Executive Director\". It tells a reader what standing the person signing has to say what the letter says."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:105
msgid "Opening paragraph"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:107
msgid "Leave empty to use the wording shown. Plain text only — bold and italic survive, other markup does not."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:115
msgid "Disclaimer"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:117
msgid "Your counsel may want particular wording, so this is yours to change. It cannot be emptied: saving it blank restores the default. A letter with no disclaimer is a letter that has quietly started implying this plugin certified something."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:125
msgid "What the reference code proves"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:127
msgid "Also cannot be emptied. Without it, a reader reasonably assumes a code means some outside body issued the document."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:137
msgid "List every shift"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:138
msgid "On by default. A total with nothing behind it is a number the reader has to take on faith, which is what this document exists to avoid."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:144
msgid "Also list hours nobody has verified"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:145
msgid "Off by default. When on, unverified shifts appear marked as such and are still excluded from the verified total — they are never quietly added in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:151
msgid "Reference prefix"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:152
msgid "Prepended to every reference code. Letters and numbers only — the code gets read aloud over the phone and typed back in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:161
msgid "Subject line"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:162
#: inc/emails.php:117
msgid "Your volunteer service verification from {org}"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:170
msgid "Covering note"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:171
msgid "Appears above the letter in the email, outside it. The letter itself is identical whether printed or emailed, and this is how a short “here is your letter” message gets added without changing the document."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:178
msgid "From name"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:179
msgid "Leave both empty to use whatever WordPress would have used."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:185
msgid "From address"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:186
msgid "Use an address at your own domain. A letter sent from an address somewhere else is the thing a spam filter is most likely to hold back, and the volunteer never learns it was sent."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:199
msgid "Issue verification letters"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:200
msgid "On unless you clear it. Clear it if your organization records hours but never writes to a court or a school: the Letters screen and the Letter settings tab disappear, and nobody can produce or send a letter. Nothing is deleted — every letter already issued, the log of what went out, and every letter setting stay exactly where they are, and selecting this again finds them unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:207
msgid "Round hours to"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:209
msgid "Do not round"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:210
msgid "5 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:211
msgid "10 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:212
msgid "15 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:213
msgid "30 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:214
msgid "A whole hour"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:216
msgid "Always to the nearest, never up — rounding up is the organization crediting hours nobody worked."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:222
msgid "Show hours as"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:224
msgid "Decimal is what a court order is usually written in."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:230
msgid "Allow shifts dated in the future"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:231
msgid "Off by default. A shift dated next Tuesday is a typo far more often than a plan, and on a document a court reads it discredits the whole record."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:237
msgid "Let volunteers send in their own hours"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:238
msgid "Off until you switch it on. With it on, this site accepts a name, an email address and a date from anonymous visitors — everything they send arrives unverified and waits for a staff member. Nothing they enter appears publicly."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:244
msgid "The page the form is on"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:245
msgid "Add the Volunteer Hours Form block, or the [gwc_vt_hours_form] shortcode, to a page and choose it here. Submissions are only accepted on this page, and it is pinned by ID so renaming it changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:251
#: inc/admin-settings.php:328
msgid "Require a code"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:252
msgid "Optional. A word you give people at the front desk, which the form then asks for. Not a security control — it is the difference between a form the whole internet can post to and one only people who have been handed a card will bother with."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:258
msgid "Keep volunteer records for"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:260
msgid "\"Keep indefinitely\" is a legitimate answer, and it is the default — a plugin that deleted records on a schedule it chose would eventually destroy the six weeks of Saturdays somebody needs for a court date. What is not legitimate is never deciding, which is why this tab nags until you save it."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:266
msgid "When a record is old enough"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:268
msgid "Remove the name and contact details, keep the hours"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:269
msgid "Delete the record and its shifts entirely"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:271
msgid "Anonymizing is usually right: your grant reporting and your Form 990 need the hours, and the hours identify nobody once the name is gone."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:277
msgid "Measured from"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:279
msgid "Their last recorded shift"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:280
msgid "The last time a shift of theirs was verified"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:282
msgid "The clock runs on the whole person, not on each shift — a record is removed when the person has been inactive this long, and their old shifts go with them. Measuring from the last shift is what most policies mean. Measuring from the last verification is later, sometimes much later, because a shift written up in March and attested in June counts from June."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:289
msgid "Activity suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:290
msgid "One per line. Offered as suggestions when logging a shift; staff can still type anything. Leave empty for free text."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:299
msgid "Plan shifts ahead of time"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:300
msgid "Off until you switch it on. With it on, a Schedule screen appears where you can plan shifts, repeat them, put volunteers on them and print a roster. A scheduled shift is a plan and records nothing about anybody's hours — hours are still logged after the fact and still have to be verified."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:307
msgid "Location suggestions"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:308
msgid "One per line. Offered as suggestions when planning a shift; you can still type anything. Leave empty for free text."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:314
msgid "Let people sign up for shifts themselves"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:315
msgid "Off until you switch it on. With it on, this site accepts a name and an email address from anonymous visitors. The public list shows what each shift is and how many places are left — never who else is coming. Nobody who signs up is added to your volunteer records automatically; a staff member matches them, exactly as with the hours form."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:321
msgid "The page the shifts are on"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:322
msgid "Add the Volunteer Shifts block, or the [gwc_vt_shift_list] shortcode, to a page and choose it here. Signups are only accepted on this page, and it is pinned by ID so renaming it changes nothing."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:329
msgid "Optional. A word you give people, which the form then asks for. Not a security control — it is the difference between a form the whole internet can post to and one only people who have been told about it will bother with."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:335
msgid "Show shifts up to"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:337
msgid "How far ahead the public list looks. A year of Saturdays is a wall of text nobody reads to the bottom of."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:343
msgid "Close signups"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:345
msgid "Right up to the start is fine for a warehouse where an extra pair of hands is always welcome. Choose earlier if you have to print a list the night before."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings.php:351
msgid "Remind people before their shift"
